rt gallery in Waigani, Port Moresby, Papua New Guinea. It is the national museum of Papua New Guinea.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Papua New Guinea National Museum and Art Gallery","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Papua_New_Guinea_National_Museum_May_2015.jpg/1280px-Papua_New_Guinea_National_Museum_May_2015.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Papua_New_Guinea_National_Museum_May_2015.jpg/500px-Papua_New_Guinea_National_Museum_May_2015.jpg","w":1200,"h":899,"author":"Nick-D","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Papua_New_Guinea_National_Museum_May_2015.jpg"}},{"id":"port_moresby_ela_beach","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Ela Beach","category":"beach","tags":["beach","sea","nature","sunset"],"location":{"lat":-9.47965,"lng":147.15616},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_ela_beach","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":3,"wikiPageviews":98,"wikidataSitelinks":3,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["elabeach","portmoresby"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Ela Beach, formerly known as Era Kone, meaning 'Turtle Beach' in the Motuan dialect of the Papuan region of Papua New Guinea, is Port Moresby's primary public beach.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Ela Beach","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Ela_Beach_May_2015.jpg/1280px-Ela_Beach_May_2015.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Ela_Beach_May_2015.jpg/500px-Ela_Beach_May_2015.jpg","w":1200,"h":900,"author":"Nick-D","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ela_Beach_May_2015.jpg"}},{"id":"port_moresby_sir_john_guise_stadium","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Sir John Guise Stadium","category":"other","tags":["family"],"location":{"lat":-9.44,"lng":147.18361},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_sir_john_guise_stadium","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":0,"wikiPageviews":538,"wikidataSitelinks":8,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["sirjohnguisestadium","portmoresby"],"summary":"The Sir John Guise Stadium is a multi-sport and athletics venue located in Port Moresby, the capital city of Papua New Guinea, and is part of the larger Sir John Guise Sports Precinct which also includes an indoor arena, beach volleyball/hockey court, and aquatics center.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Sir John Guise Stadium","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/Sir._John_Guise_Stadium.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/fd/Sir._John_Guise_Stadium.jpg","w":1200,"h":789,"author":"derivative work: Rhinen","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir._John_Guise_Stadium.jpg"}},{"id":"port_moresby_sir_hubert_murray_stadium","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Sir Hubert Murray Stadium","category":"other","tags":["family"],"location":{"lat":-9.46694,"lng":147.15667},"visitMinutes":90,"priceLevel":2,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_sir_hubert_murray_stadium","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":0,"commonsNearby":1,"wikiPageviews":223,"wikidataSitelinks":9,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["sirhubertmurraystadium","portmoresby"],"summary":"The Hubert Murray Stadium is a sports venue located in Port Moresby, the capital city of Papua New Guinea. It was developed for the 1969 South Pacific Games on reclaimed land at Konedobu that had previously been shoreline mangroves.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Sir Hubert Murray Stadium","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Sir_Hubert_Murray_Stadium_%281993%2C_cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Sir_Hubert_Murray_Stadium_%281993%2C_cropped%29.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Sir_Hubert_Murray_Stadium_%281993%2C_cropped%29.jpg/500px-Sir_Hubert_Murray_Stadium_%281993%2C_cropped%29.jpg","w":1200,"h":664,"author":"lindsaybridge","license":"CC BY 2.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir_Hubert_Murray_Stadium_(1993,_cropped).jpg"}},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_national_parliament_of_papua_new_guinea","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"National Parliament of Papua New Guinea","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-9.42806,"lng":147.19191},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_national_parliament_of_papua_new_guinea","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["nationalparliamentofpapuanewguinea","portmoresby"],"summary":"Parliament Haus is one of the most impressive buildings in Port Moresby, built in the style of a Maprik Haus Tambaran (house of spirits from East Sepik Province). Dating from 1984, it is usually open to visitors.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_touaguba_hill","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Touaguba Hill","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-9.47478,"lng":147.15983},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_touaguba_hill","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["touagubahill","portmoresby"],"summary":"Perhaps not so much to see, but this is where the ambassadorial residences are located and is also where many of the well-to-do expats and locals live. There is a nice view from the top of the hill overlooking the centre of the city and the ocean.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_port_moresby_golf_club","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Port Moresby Golf Club","category":"landmark","tags":["photo"],"location":{"lat":-9.42357,"lng":147.1917},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":1,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_port_moresby_golf_club","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["portmoresbygolfclub","portmoresby"],"summary":"A nice golf course located right across from the government buildings. The prices are quite acceptable for visitors. Be careful: crocodiles inhabit the water holes of the golf course. The main building has a nice restaurant where one can have lunch and have a few SP beers (South Pacific beers) after a round of golf.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_ela_beach_craft_market","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Ela Beach Craft Market","category":"beach","tags":["beach","sea","nature","sunset"],"location":{"lat":-9.48112,"lng":147.15175},"visitMinutes":120,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_ela_beach_craft_market","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsNearby":0,"wikidataSitelinks":0,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-20"},"hashtags":["elabeachcraftmarket","portmoresby"],"bestLight":"sunset","summary":"Run by the Ela Murray International School and held on the last Saturday of each month, this market brings together local artifacts from all over Papua New Guinea. An easy way to get some beautiful carvings, handwoven baskets, or any of a number of other things to bring home as souvenirs.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_duffy_cafe","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Duffy Cafe","category":"cafe","tags":["cafes"],"location":{"lat":-9.47718,"lng":147.1489},"visitMinutes":45,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_duffy_cafe","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://duffypng.com/","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["duffycafe","portmoresby"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"},{"open":"08:00","close":"18:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"bestLight":"morning","summary":"PNG's premiere cafe, making great use of the local beans and also serving good food. Main location is in Harbour Side but there are other branches, including in the international terminal departure lounge.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_royal_papua_yacht_club","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Royal Papua Yacht Club","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-9.46634,"lng":147.15479},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_royal_papua_yacht_club","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["royalpapuayachtclub","portmoresby"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"Serves good Australian cuisine with some Papua New Guinean touches. Has à la carte menu and a buffet that varies according to the day of the week. An invitation from a member might be required to enter.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_lamana_hotel","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Lamana Hotel","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-9.44232,"lng":147.18},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_lamana_hotel","tickets":[{"vendor":"Official","url":"http://www.lamanahotel.com.pg/","official":true}],"signals":{},"hashtags":["lamanahotel","portmoresby"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"A nice place for a quick lunch buffet with friendly staff and a happening casino at night. The food is good and the only place where you get Indian food.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_daikoku","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Daikoku","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-9.46399,"lng":147.15479},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_daikoku","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["daikokuportmoresby","portmoresby"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"It offers great Japanese cuisine cooked directly at your table (teppanyaki). Don't forget to try the \"Puk Puk\" which is Tok Pisin for crocodile.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_beachside_brasserie","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Beachside Brasserie","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-9.47945,"lng":147.15485},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_beachside_brasserie","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["beachsidebrasserie","portmoresby"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"The hotel restaurant is well-appointed and has an extensive menu, especially grills and seafood. Also great for breakfast.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Port Moresby"},{"id":"port_moresby_wv_jacksons_bar_and_restaurant","areaId":"port_moresby","name":"Jacksons Bar and Restaurant","category":"food","tags":["food"],"location":{"lat":-9.44762,"lng":147.21427},"visitMinutes":75,"photoSeed":"port_moresby_wv_jacksons_bar_and_restaurant","tickets":[],"signals":{},"hashtags":["jacksonsbarandrestaurant","portmoresby"],"hours":{"week":[{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"},{"open":"12:00","close":"22:00"}],"note":"Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"A complex in the Gateway Hotel, overlooking the airport. Their best thing is crispy-base pizzas.","summarySource":"wikivoyage","wikivoyageTitle":"en:Port Moresby"}],"sources":["Wikidata (CC0)","Wikimedia Commons (counts; photos credited per file)","Wikipedia (pageviews; summaries CC BY-SA 4.0)","Wikivoyage (listings: hours, prices, descriptions; CC BY-SA 4.0)","OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL): opening hours, fees, websites"]}